### **Marketing Strategy**
The Company's marketing strategy targets both regular and potential customers. When it specifically comes to its regulars, the Company makes use of the following marketing strategies:
- Providing them with technical services/support for existing products and product development for customers;
- 2. Hosting regular meetings with customers to strengthen relationships and foster customer loyalty. The Company also participates in the Indonesia Olefin, Aromatic and Plastics Industry Association (INAPLAS) to bridge the relationship gap between customers, consultants, industry, and the government;
- Improving its product quality by nutruing cooperation and communication between the production, product development and marketing teams, as well as with the business development and quality assurance departments. Through this process, customers are also involved as a means to provide the Company with inputs related to product quality consistency through annual surveys;
- Providing satellite warehouses in East Java and Central Java to shorten delivery time to customers;
- 5. Menyediakan bentuk kemasan sesuai permintaan pasar untuk membantu pelanggan kami agar bisa mencapai tingkat efisiensi operasional yang lebih tinggi serta penghematan biaya;
- 6. Mempercepat transformasi digital di seluruh departemen untuk meningkatkan efisiensi, efektivitas, dan visibilitas sehingga kami dapat memberikan respons yang lebih cepat, lebih akurat, dan meningkatkan kepuasan pelanggan secara keseluruhan;
- 7. Melakukan survei kepuasan pelanggan setiap tahun, yang bertujuan untuk mengevaluasi kinerja pelayanan pelanggan.
Sedangkan untuk calon pelanggan, Perseroan melaksanakan strategi pemasaran sebagai berikut:
- 1. Memberikan pelayanan/pelatihan teknis bagi calon pelanggan dalam memproduksi dan mengembangkan produk;
- 2. Melakukan riset pemasaran yang bertujuan untuk mengeksplorasi peluang yang terkait dengan potensi pelanggan;

